    <div class="bio-content">
      <span class="section-eyebrow">Meet Sheri</span>
      <h1>I used to feel<br /><em>intimidated too.</em></h1>
      <p>
        Hi, I'm Sheri — a working mom of two girls, a Respiratory Therapist, and a passionate
        home DIYer based in South Surrey, BC.
      </p>
      <p>
        Since 2017 I've been updating our fixer-uppers — first our townhouse, and now our detached
        home. I learned alongside my husband and dad, and for a long time I felt completely out of
        my depth. <strong>The intimidation was real.</strong>
      </p>
      <p>
        After years of learning, making mistakes, and figuring it out room by room — I'm passionate
        about making sure other women don't have to feel that way.
        <strong>You don't need experience. You don't need a contractor. You just need someone to show you how.</strong>
      </p>
      <div class="bio-stats">
        <div class="bio-stat">
          <span class="bio-stat-num">7+</span>
          <span class="bio-stat-label">Years DIYing</span>
        </div>
        <div class="bio-stat">
          <span class="bio-stat-num">2</span>
          <span class="bio-stat-label">Homes Transformed</span>
        </div>
        <div class="bio-stat">
          <span class="bio-stat-num">100%</span>
          <span class="bio-stat-label">Beginner Friendly</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <a href="/work-with-me" class="btn-primary">Work With Me</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="story-section">
    <h2>Why I started <em>Home DIYs for Busy Women</em></h2>
    <p>
      When we bought our first fixer-upper townhouse, I had zero experience. My husband was handy,
      my dad had always done projects around the house, but I'd never picked up a caulking gun in
      my life. I was a healthcare professional — I could handle a lot — but a paintbrush felt
      surprisingly intimidating.
    </p>

    <div class="pull-quote">
      <p>"I kept waiting to feel ready. Eventually I realized the only way to feel ready was to just start."</p>
    </div>

    <p>
      I started small. Painted a bathroom. Fixed a drywall hole that had been staring at me for
      months. Caulked the baseboards. And slowly, project by project, I stopped being scared
      of my own house.
    </p>
    <p>
      The transformation wasn't just in the walls — it was in me. I started to feel capable in a
      space where I'd always felt like I was just borrowing someone else's skills. That feeling
      became something I couldn't stop thinking about sharing.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>That's why Home DIYs for Busy Women exists.</strong> Because there are so many women out there
      with a Pinterest board full of ideas and no idea where to start. Women who don't want to
      wait for a contractor, pay a contractor, or depend on someone else to make their home
      feel like theirs.
    </p>
    <p>
      I'm not a professional contractor. I'm a mom who figured it out — and now I'm here to
      make sure you can too.
    </p>
  </div>

